& [SelectedIntent] is the next dependency-ready non-effect scanner prerequisite
  + [purpose] is decide whether already observed Windows entry metadata is admissible before traversal or content interpretation
  + [input] is entry kind, raw u32 attributes, per-directory case-sensitivity flags, exact Unicode component, and caller-supplied component bound
  + [output] is one admitted pure policy record or one closed policy fault
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-entry-policy/0.1

& [AttributeIntent] is fail closed
  + [benign_bits] are READONLY, HIDDEN, SYSTEM, ARCHIVE, and NOT_CONTENT_INDEXED
  + [directory] requires DIRECTORY and otherwise permits only benign bits
  + [regular] permits NORMAL alone or one nonempty subset of benign bits
  + [zero_unknown_behavior_kind_mismatch] reject
  + [case_flags] must equal zero for a directory

& [NameIntent] is strict
  + [characters] reject NUL, controls U+0001 through U+001F, less-than, greater-than, colon, quote, slash, backslash, vertical-bar, question-mark, and asterisk
  + [terminal] rejects trailing space or period
  + [components] reject empty, dot, dot-dot, and .git under ordinal ASCII case-insensitive comparison
  + [devices] reject CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1 through COM9, LPT1 through LPT9, and COM or LPT followed by superscript 1, 2, or 3, including when followed by an extension
  + [Unicode] preserves exact scalar values and performs no normalization
  + [ordering] compares exact UTF-8 bytes

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure only
  - never: call Win32, inspect a path or handle, traverse, read content, enumerate streams, create a receipt, infer Git mode, mutate, or claim target-host behavior
  - never: treat this source as implementation authority until SJS produces a signed canonical specification

